      "name": "PostQuantum.KeyManagement",
      "version": "0.4.0-preview.2",
      "description": "Clean, high-level key management and rotation for post-quantum-ready encryption in .NET. Implements the envelope-encryption pattern (256-bit content keys wrapped by a key-encryption key) with a secure local KEK provider backed by Argon2id \u002B AES-256-GCM, full thread-safety, hostile-input-resistant token parsers, an HMAC-SHA256 keyring verifier for early passphrase detection, first-class Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection integration (AddPostQuantumKeyManagement, IKeyringStore \u002B atomic FileKeyringStore, KeyManagementHealthCheck), and a tiny extension point so cloud KMS providers (Azure Key Vault, AWS KMS, Google Cloud KMS, PKCS#11/HSMs) plug in as separate packages without disturbing application code. The natural companion to PostQuantum.FileEncryption and PostQuantum.Jwt. See KNOWN-GAPS.md and docs/threat-model.md for honest, explicit limits.",
